  {"rows": [0..999]}
    python render_value -> {"kind":"json", data.rows length 200, note "1 array(s) truncated to the first 200 entries; original lengths: [1000]"}
    js     materialize   -> {"kind":"json", data.rows length 1000, note null}
  {"a":{"b":[[0..299]]}}
    python -> truncated to 200, note "original lengths: [300]"
    js     -> untouched, note null
  [0..999] (top level) -> both truncate to 200 (this is the only shape they agree on).
Harness: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-DiscStudio-staging/c7ad5950-a39c-58bb-9747-e1301075cf94/scratchpad/adv/cross.mjs and the matching inline python3 run. A 1000-row Part nested one level down — the ordinary shape of every grouped-ablation value — is a 200-row record in pyto and a 1000-row record in the browser, with no note in the browser saying anything was left whole.
